  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities Living Peacefully - Centro Montalvo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive and sensitive conflict and gender analysis Border communities, migrants and other stakeholders have increased capacity to address environmental protection challenges and have developed plans towards environmental protection Initiatives implemented to protect and manage the environment Advocacy actions for public policies on environmental management along the border A conflict analysis on human trafficking, smuggling and prejudices in the border context is undertaken. Inclusive and sensitive conflict and gender analysis Stronger capacity for conflict resolution amongst key stakeholders in border communities and at national level in Haiti and DR Establishing a platform where civil society organizations, the State and UN actors can liaise and work more effectively with the local authorities on existing tensions related to trafficking and migration in both Haiti and the Dominican Republic A joint communication and advocacy campaign on migration issues to promote cohesion, respect and peacebuilding is organized. The number of migrants and people under 18 with civil registration has increased Educational institutions enable undocumented children to study in both the Haitian and Dominican education systems</narrative>
  </description>
